{"id": "EUVD-2026-108125", "enisaUuid": "5bcc4312-ff60-3576-a932-d554a3b42991", "description": "EverShop 1.2.2 before 2.2.1 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the customer address API that allows unauthenticated attackers to manage other customers' addresses. Attackers who know customer and address UUIDs can send POST, PATCH, or DELETE requests to /api/customers/:customer_id/addresses routes to add, modify, or delete saved shipping addresses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:42", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/evershopcommerce/evershop/issues/928", "https://github.com/evershopcommerce/evershop/commit/af6e6fd935c4194668b11a924b847542598941f7", "https://github.com/evershopcommerce/evershop/releases/tag/v2.2.1", "https://github.com/evershopcommerce/evershop/blob/v2.1.2/packages/evershop/src/modules/customer/api/updateCustomerAddress/updateCustomerAddress.js", "https://github.com/evershopcommerce/evershop/blob/v2.1.2/packages/evershop/src/modules/customer/api/deleteCustomerAddress/route.json", "https://github.com/evershopcommerce/evershop", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/evershop-1.2.2-before-2.2.1-missing-authorization-via-customer-address-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115323", "GHSA-9rjv-95rj-93cg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "109110aa-297b-3d3f-a363-f102166ae685", "product": {"name": "EverShop", "vendor": {"name": "evershopcommerce"}}, "product_version": "1.2.2 <2.2.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "835a40ef-79bf-3985-b8cd-8b244c19ad33", "vendor": {"name": "evershopcommerce"}}], "isExploited": false}